# Line endings are part of what this project tests, so they must not depend on the machine.
#
# ManifestJson.Serialize writes a bare \n on purpose: the Mac build this port follows ends a
# pretty-printed line the same way, and taking the platform default would make every save on
# Windows a whole-file diff against a project a Mac wrote. Tests that compare against raw string
# literals inherit their line endings from the source file, so a checkout that arrives as CRLF
# makes those expectations disagree with the writer. Keep every text file LF so the checkout is
# identical everywhere, and the test that broke in CI cannot break that way again.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats: never touch their bytes.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.skn binary
*.ttf binary
*.packet binary
